{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-23503-r4630392","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Brazilian Shrimp and Cassava Sauce (Bobó de Camarao)","sourcePageId":23503,"sourceRevision":"4630392","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T21:52:24Z","sourceRevisionUser":"AdoniTzedek","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Brazilian%20Shrimp%20and%20Cassava%20Sauce%20(Bob%C3%B3%20de%20Camarao)&oldid=4630392","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:45.135Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Brazilian recipes","Category:Halal recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Pescatarian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using cassava","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using coconut milk","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using shrimp","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"11a7faef56ccc7be2388864902ca7f8c2602af05372e48c98fc39a733e307f7c","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Brazilian recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}| [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Brazil|Brazilian Cuisine]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Pound|lbs]] (1.2 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]]) medium size [[Cookbook:Shrimp|shrimp]]\n* 3 lb (1.2 kg) [[Cookbook:Cassava|yuca root]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 3 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], chopped\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n* 6 medium [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], peeled and seeded (or a large can of whole tomatoes)\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Cilantro|cilantro]], chopped\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Coconut Milk|coconut milk]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Palm Oil|palm oil]] (also known as dendê)\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n\n==Preparation==\n\n#Peel and cut the manioc and put in a pan with cold water and salt.\n#Cook until tender, drain and reserve both the cooked manioc and the liquid.\n#Discard any manioc fiber.\n#Using a fork, mash the manioc while still hot. Use some of the liquid to help in the process. Do not use a blender or food processor.\n#Peel and de-vein the shrimp.\n#[[Cookbook:Sauté|Sauté]] the onion and garlic in the olive oil until wilted.\n#Add ½ of the chopped cilantro and the tomatoes, stirring well.\n#Add the shrimp, and cook it for about 15 minutes.\n#Add the [[Cookbook:Purée|puréed]] manioc. Check the amount of liquid and add more of the reserved manioc liquid to thin the mixture, if necessary.\n#Add the coconut milk, the remaining cilantro and the palm oil.\n#Check for salt and pepper.\n#Serve over Brazilian white rice.\n\n[[Category:Pescatarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes]]\n[[Category:Brazilian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cassava]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Brazilian Shrimp and Cassava Sauce (Bobó de Camarao)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 lbs (1.2 kg) medium size shrimp","sourceText":"3 lbs (1.2 kg) medium size shrimp","am